title: Synology Active Backup for Microsoft 365
agents: special
catalog: applications
license: MIT
distribution: DanielDietz-de
description:
 Monitors Synology Active Backup for Microsoft 365 through the authenticated JSON
 API provided by the separately installed synology-activebackup-zabbixmonitor DSM
 package. The Checkmk integration does not read or modify Synology backup databases
 directly.

 The special agent retrieves one complete /api/v1/status snapshot per execution.
 A permanent Health service monitors the Microsoft 365 source, product-scoped
 collection errors, and collector freshness. The upstream collector health object
 is global across all enabled products; this check therefore does not make an M365
 service CRIT solely because an unrelated ABB or Hyper Backup database is missing.

 One additional itemized service is discovered for each Microsoft 365 task_id. The
 technical task_id is used as persistent service identity; the human-readable backup
 job name is display information only.

 Normalized upstream states are mapped as follows: successful and running jobs are
 OK, warnings/partial/skipped jobs are WARN, failed jobs and missing M365 databases
 are CRIT, no-data jobs are WARN, and unmapped states are UNKNOWN. Independently of
 the current run state, the service checks the age of the last fully successful run.
 The default levels assume daily backups: WARN after 30 hours and CRIT after 48
 hours. Warning or partially completed runs do not reset the last-success timer.
 These levels are configurable through the service parameter rule.

 Metrics cover collector age, latest-run age, last-success age, runtime, and
 transferred bytes.

 The collector API uses HTTP by default. Production use requires a protected
 management path and strict source filtering until a verified TLS deployment path
 is enabled and tested.

inventory:
 One health service is always discovered. One additional service is discovered for
 every valid Microsoft 365 task_id returned by the collector.
